  "chunks": [
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Architectural Engineering (هندسة العمارة) — B.Sc. study plan 2025/2026, Faculty of Engineering & Design, Middle East University.\nThe degree requires 165 credit hours in total:\n- University requirements: 18 credit hours (compulsory)\n- University electives: 6 credit hours\n- Faculty requirements: 24 credit hours (group A: 6, group C: 18 — freehand drawing, computer design applications, aesthetics, history of art and architecture, basic design, psychology and sociology of design)\n- Area of study (major) requirements: 99 credit hours, including six Architectural Design studios (4 credit hours each)\n- Ancillary courses: 6 credit hours (Mathematics I, Physics I)\n- Area of study (major) electives: 12 credit hours\nRemedial courses are taken only when required and are not counted in the 165 hours.\nThe plan includes Field Practice (320 training hours, after 110 completed credit hours) and a two-part graduation project (Graduation Project 1 after 120 completed credit hours and Architectural Design 6)."
    },
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Architectural Engineering study plan 2025/2026 — approvals and signatories.\nFaculty Council decision 05/06-2025/2026, adopted 06/11/2025. Deans' Council decision 10/15-2025/2026, adopted 30/12/2025.\nHead of Department: Dr. Mohammad Hamdan. Dean of the Faculty: Prof. Ayman Abdel Salam Awad. Director of Admissions and Registration: Mrs. Nadia Al-Bakri."
    },
    {
      "category": "study_plan",
      "lang": "en",
      "text": "Architectural Engineering — digital and sustainable design courses in the 2025/2026 study plan:\nComputer Application in Architecture 1 and 2 (1932301/1933301), Green Architecture and Sustainable Design (العمارة الخضراء والتصميم المستدام, 1933701), Environmental Control (1933702), Lighting and Acoustics in Architecture (1934501), Landscape Architecture (1933901), Urban Design and Planning (1934901). Electives include Architectural Visualization, Introduction to Parametric Design in Architecture, Certificate in Digital Architectural Design 1, Architectural Modeling and Simulation, Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design, Design for Greater Efficiency and Theories of Conservation of Architectural Heritage."
    }
  ],
